    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3fe94e76-5fda-51ed-9445-3ba609a531c4" activityNameId="6fdf8e2e-216e-5e70-b2e9-ae908765adb1" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Mouse device, optical, wireless, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Mouse device, optical, wireless, at plant
The dataset is made from the existing average mice; UUID: ae6e6500-bb34-3fa6-a85a-91eac465271b
The wireless mouse is modeled using the existing wired mouse dataset. The modifications to the existing mice include the addition of a single NiMh battery (25 grams), the removal of wired cable, and lastly the increased mass of PCB components (Babbitt et al., 2020). The rest of other inventory flows are assumed to be the same as optimized wired mice - see the mentioned dataset.
Location: Data for global average wireless mice
Technology: The production of an optical mouse includes the sheet rolling of the steel plate plus the injection moulding of the plastic and rubber parts (cover, base and wheel).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature data and own assumptions for processing calculations.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ae6e6500-bb34-3fa6-a85a-91eac465271b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
